    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d175">

                <pb facs="0221" n="1055" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1055"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/9935</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-06T12:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 6, 1918—noon.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5517. For McFadden [from War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 291. Embassy’s 4892, August 27, 6 p.m., your 372.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d175-f1"/> War Trade Board’s position in matter in question entirely
                    set forth in Department’s No. 5506, our 287, September 4, 3 p.m. To make
                    definite War Trade Board’s position reference scope of conference <pb
                        facs="0222" n="1056" xml:id="pg1056"/> activities, as intended and
                    considered desirable by War Trade Board and by Washington representatives of
                    French, English, Italian Governments, conference will consider all cases where
                    normal action of Government concerned would be restriction of transaction owing
                    to enemy character or affiliation of a person involved therein.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
